.TH NGSPICE-DOCKER 1 "March 2026" "IHP macOS Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ngspice-docker \- Run ngspice with OSDI/Verilog-A support via Docker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ngspice-docker
[\fB\-b\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIlogfile\fR]
.I netlist.sp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ngspice-docker
is a wrapper script that runs ngspice inside a Docker container to provide
OSDI and Verilog-A model support on macOS, where native compilation is problematic.

The script automatically translates macOS file paths to container paths and
manages Docker volume mounts.
.SH PREREQUISITES
.SS Environment Configuration
Before using
.BR ngspice-docker ,
ensure your shell environment is properly configured:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
.EE
.in
.PP
This loads:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
TOOLKIT_ROOT (path to ihp-macos-toolkit)
.IP \(bu 2
PDK_ROOT (path to IHP-Open-PDK)
.IP \(bu 2
PDK=ihp-sg13g2
.IP \(bu 2
Adds toolkit scripts to PATH
.RE
.PP
Verify environment:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
echo $TOOLKIT_ROOT
which ngspice-docker
.EE
.in
.SS Docker Desktop
Docker must be running before executing
.BR ngspice-docker .
.PP
.B Check Docker status:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
docker info
.EE
.in
.PP
If this fails:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Launch Docker Desktop from Applications
.IP 2.
Wait for the Docker icon (whale) to stabilize in menu bar
.IP 3.
Verify again with
.B docker info
.RE
.SS Verify Installation
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Check script is in PATH
which ngspice-docker

# Should display:
# /path/to/ihp-macos-toolkit/scripts/ngspice-docker

# Test Docker connectivity
docker run --rm hello-world
.EE
.in
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Batch mode. Run netlist without interactive shell.
.TP
.BI \-o " logfile"
Write output to
.IR logfile .
Path translation is automatic.
.TP
.I netlist.sp
SPICE netlist to simulate. Can use absolute or relative paths.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Simulation
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ngspice-docker circuit.sp
.EE
.in
.SS Batch Mode with Log
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ngspice-docker -b -o results.log amplifier.sp
.EE
.in
.SS Using PDK Models
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# In your netlist:
.include /pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib

# Run normally
ngspice-docker -b my_design.sp
.EE
.in
.PP
The
.B /pdk
path is automatically mounted from $PDK_ROOT.
.SH AUTOMATIC PATH TRANSLATION
The wrapper automatically translates macOS paths to Docker container paths:
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
macOS Path|Container Path
_
$PDK_ROOT|/pdk
$(pwd)|/work
T{
.na
Any file in current directory or subdirectories
T}|T{
.na
Accessible in /work
T}
.TE
.PP
You can use both macOS paths (in your shell) and container paths (in netlists).
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Command not found
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Check PATH
echo $PATH | grep toolkit

# If missing, reload environment
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
.EE
.in
.SS Docker connection refused
.PP
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Launch Docker Desktop
.IP 2.
Wait for icon to become stable (not animated)
.IP 3.
Verify:
.B docker ps
.RE
.SS Permission denied
.PP
Ensure Docker Desktop has necessary permissions in System Preferences > Privacy & Security.
.SS Model files not found
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Verify PDK_ROOT is set
echo $PDK_ROOT

# Should point to IHP-Open-PDK installation
# Check models exist
ls $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/
.EE
.in
.SS Simulation hangs
.PP
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Check Docker has sufficient resources (Preferences > Resources)
.IP \(bu 2
Verify netlist syntax with native ngspice first (if available)
.IP \(bu 2
Check Docker logs:
.B docker logs
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/ngspice-docker
The wrapper script
.TP
.I $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
Environment configuration file
.TP
.I $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/
SPICE models and libraries
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOOLKIT_ROOT
Path to ihp-macos-toolkit installation
.TP
.B PDK_ROOT
Path to IHP-Open-PDK installation
.TP
.B PDK
PDK name (should be "ihp-sg13g2")
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Temporary directory for intermediate files (optional, defaults to /tmp)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ngspice (1),
.BR docker (1)
.PP
